    "api_note": "In python, current_data.put(key, value) stores a JSON value for the current observation; current_data.get(key) returns {status, value, written_at} only when status=='current'. Other statuses contain no saved value. Values survive snippets, but any executed action (including no-op or RESET) makes them stale. For example: entry=current_data.get('measurement'); value=entry['value'] if entry['status']=='current' else None. Optionally obtain at=current_data.context()['context'] before computing, then put(key, value, at=at); a changed observation rejects this write. A stored response confirms a host commit, including if the snippet later fails or times out; missing acknowledgment means the write outcome is unknown. written_at identifies the observation at commit, not the value's source or correctness. Previously read local aliases do not auto-invalidate. JSON only: null/bool/int/finite float/string/list/dict with string keys; no objects, tuples, cycles or depth over 16. Default limits are 16 KiB/value, 64 KiB/session and 32 keys; keys are nonempty strings of at most 128 UTF-8 bytes. Rejected writes preserve existing valid values. No value is printed automatically.",
    "semantics": {
      "binding": "Host observation at commit; does not prove value source or correctness.",
      "invalidation": "Any executed action including no-op/RESET; get/put recheck live host identity.",
      "commit": "Synchronous host replacement before IPC ack; no snippet-end commit or rollback. Unacknowledged write is unknown.",
      "aliases": "Each get is a JSON copy; previously returned local aliases cannot auto-invalidate.",
      "bytes": "Canonical UTF-8 JSON value bytes, not RSS; keys/stale metadata separately bounded.",
      "hash": "SHA256 canonical sorted-key compact UTF-8 JSON. Frame hash uses compact settled grid JSON.",
      "cpu": "Host thread CPU for query/action-boundary bookkeeping, excluding original actions and child validation.",
      "eviction": "FIFO sessions; no resurrection. Up to max_keys current or stale records; new keys reject when full."
    }
  },
